(mimics spy music)

2068
01:21:32,555 --> 01:21:37,893
Uh, this really
bulks up my pecs.

2069
01:21:37,927 --> 01:21:38,862
Hey!

2070
01:21:38,895 --> 01:21:39,862
Go get him.

2071
01:21:39,895 --> 01:21:40,897
Get him!

2072
01:21:40,930 --> 01:21:43,198
Man, you guys are getting
into this, aren't ya?

2073
01:21:43,232 --> 01:21:45,302
Well, you know.

2074
01:21:45,335 --> 01:21:47,270
Stay away from
him, you bitches.

2075
01:21:47,303 --> 01:21:52,008
Uh, camera two,
clear the shot please.

2076
01:21:52,042 --> 01:21:55,178
(laughs)

2077
01:21:55,212 --> 01:21:58,682
Spotlight dance, Richard Kiel.

2078
01:21:58,715 --> 01:22:04,020
(all hum)

2079
01:22:04,053 --> 01:22:10,460
Doesn't do much but it
sure lights the place, huh?

2080
01:22:10,493 --> 01:22:14,197
These guys are little,
but they'll crawl ya.

2081
01:22:14,230 --> 01:22:17,800
They're getting board.

2082
01:22:17,833 --> 01:22:22,738
Wait, Otto
Preminger's getting away.

2083
01:22:22,772 --> 01:22:25,942
Timber!

2084
01:22:25,975 --> 01:22:30,447
(dramatic classical music)

2085
01:22:30,480 --> 01:22:31,948
Wait a minute, they're
fighting each other

2086
01:22:31,982 --> 01:22:33,015
all of a sudden.

2087
01:22:33,048 --> 01:22:34,450
I don't get this.

2088
01:22:34,483 --> 01:22:36,018
I think it's the
end of the movie.

2089
01:22:36,052 --> 01:22:39,922
Oh.

2090
01:22:39,955 --> 01:22:41,758
No, stop, you're killing me.

2091
01:22:41,792 --> 01:22:42,958
(laughs)

2092
01:22:42,992 --> 01:22:44,760
This is weird.

2093
01:22:44,793 --> 01:22:46,863
These progressive
dance clubs are getting

2094
01:22:46,897 --> 01:22:49,465
out of hand.

2095
01:22:49,498 --> 01:22:51,802
Gentlemen, gentlemen, ooh.

2096
01:22:51,835 --> 01:22:55,938
Ow!

2097
01:22:55,972 --> 01:23:00,377
I am so ashamed.

2098
01:23:00,410 --> 01:23:05,982
Oh, lost my head over that one.

2099
01:23:06,015 --> 01:23:09,418
Dog pile on me, yay.

2100
01:23:09,452 --> 01:23:12,022
Just got to run to the
biffy, be right back.

2101
01:23:12,055 --> 01:23:16,358
Not an android, just
walking, calmly walking.

2102
01:23:16,392 --> 01:23:18,362
I've been spending
all movie inside

2103
01:23:18,395 --> 01:23:19,962
and it's beautiful out here.

2104
01:23:19,995 --> 01:23:22,532
Damn, mom's here.

2105
01:23:22,565 --> 01:23:29,005
(humming "Axel F")

2106
01:23:29,038 --> 01:23:31,975
I'm Howard Kiel, no
relation to Richard Kiel.

2107
01:23:32,008 --> 01:23:37,580
(dramatic classical music)

2108
01:23:37,613 --> 01:23:40,617
Finally, we meet
in the living room.

2109
01:23:44,820 --> 01:23:46,622
Don't try it,
they're decorative.

2110
01:23:46,655 --> 01:23:48,123
Be your last.

2111
01:23:48,157 --> 01:23:49,958
Your threats do not alarm me.

2112
01:23:49,992 --> 01:23:50,827
Okay they do.

2113
01:23:50,860 --> 01:23:53,362
You forget, I know no fear.

2114
01:23:53,397 --> 01:23:55,332
Androids have no
emotions, Martin.

2115
01:23:55,365 --> 01:23:56,598
Look what happened.

2116
01:23:56,632 --> 01:23:58,133
Hey, wipe my feet.

2117
01:23:58,167 --> 01:24:01,037
Professor Dornheimer, I
was not correctly programmed.

2118
01:24:01,070 --> 01:24:03,873
No duplicate of mine
is going to say that.

2119
01:24:03,907 --> 01:24:05,608
I must see the master.

2120
01:24:05,642 --> 01:24:07,610
I am the master here.

2121
01:24:07,643 --> 01:24:08,945
Do as I command you.

2122
01:24:08,978 --> 01:24:10,012
Not as I do.

2123
01:24:10,045 --> 01:24:11,815
Destroy this human being.

2124
01:24:11,848 --> 01:24:14,483
(dramatic classical music)

2125
01:24:14,517 --> 01:24:15,952
That is my twin.

2126
01:24:15,985 --> 01:24:17,687
We are not humans.

2127
01:24:17,720 --> 01:24:19,088
He is our enemy.

2128
01:24:19,122 --> 01:24:20,657
Kill him.

2129
01:24:20,690 --> 01:24:23,125
I want this "you"
situation taken care of.

2130
01:24:23,158 --> 01:24:25,262
I command you.

2131
01:24:25,295 --> 01:24:27,463
I am your master.

2132
01:24:27,497 --> 01:24:28,998
No, Kolos is the master.

2133
01:24:29,032 --> 01:24:30,667
I obey no other.

2134
01:24:30,700 --> 01:24:32,768
You stupid mechanical...

2135
01:24:32,802 --> 01:24:34,670
No Dad, not the belt.

2136
01:24:34,703 --> 01:24:40,743
Ow, my GI Joe arm. Ow.

2137
01:24:40,777 --> 01:24:43,480
The gloves are off, they're
tied up against the boards.

2138
01:24:43,513 --> 01:24:47,317
Lou Nanne is running
in to break it up.

2139
01:24:47,350 --> 01:24:49,918
Yeah, yeah that's the
spot, right there, yeah.

2140
01:24:49,952 --> 01:24:53,923
Hit him in the head,
they've got Hummel heads.

2141
01:24:53,957 --> 01:24:56,125
Virginia Grim,
thank God we're saved.

2142
01:24:56,158 --> 01:25:02,598
Did we come at a bad time?

2143
01:25:02,632 --> 01:25:06,302
Darling.

2144
01:25:06,335 --> 01:25:09,238
They died as they lived,
in each others arms.

2145
01:25:09,272 --> 01:25:11,140
But for GI Joe and
his fighting force,

2146
01:25:11,173 --> 01:25:13,308
there would be another day.

2147
01:25:13,342 --> 01:25:14,977
Eww.

2148
01:25:15,010 --> 01:25:17,813
Oh no, he's going to take
her to the tower, isn't he?

2149
01:25:17,847 --> 01:25:26,655
Did we get everything here?

2150
01:25:26,688 --> 01:25:27,490
(mimics thud)

2151
01:25:27,523 --> 01:25:28,423
Ow.

2152
01:25:28,457 --> 01:25:31,660
Sorry about your
head, I think.

2153
01:25:31,693 --> 01:25:34,997
Exit, stage left.

2154
01:25:35,030 --> 01:25:36,298
Somebody want to say
something, it's kind

2155
01:25:36,332 --> 01:25:41,905
of dragging here.

2156
01:25:41,938 --> 01:25:47,177
Someone drop this?

2157
01:25:47,210 --> 01:25:49,112
The hell?

2158
01:25:49,145 --> 01:25:50,112
Mr. Martin.

2159
01:25:50,145 --> 01:25:51,480
Call me Steve.

2160
01:25:51,513 --> 01:25:54,183
I was sent here to prepare
you society for conquest

2161
01:25:54,217 --> 01:25:56,252
by the masters of the galaxy.

2162
01:25:56,285 --> 01:25:57,720
But it didn't really pan out.

2163
01:25:57,753 --> 01:25:58,688
I have failed in my mission.

2164
01:25:58,722 --> 01:26:00,357
Big time.

2165
01:26:00,390 --> 01:26:02,225
I have failed not
because I am weak.

2166
01:26:02,258 --> 01:26:04,927
But because you are stronger.

2167
01:26:04,960 --> 01:26:07,597
I will leave your planet now.

2168
01:26:07,630 --> 01:26:10,367
I must return to a world of cold

2169
01:26:10,400 --> 01:26:13,002
and unemotional galaxy beings.

2170
01:26:13,035 --> 01:26:14,170
Minnesota?

2171
01:26:14,203 --> 01:26:16,305
I will give them my report

2172
01:26:16,338 --> 01:26:17,973
and then I will be destroyed

2173
01:26:18,007 --> 01:26:19,775
But enough about me.

2174
01:26:19,808 --> 01:26:21,310
But it will not matter.
You see, Mr. Martin,

2175
01:26:21,343 --> 01:26:25,815
I know now that I,
too, am an android.

2176
01:26:25,848 --> 01:26:28,785
Well, I didn't think they
piled human stuff that high.

2177
01:26:28,818 --> 01:26:30,520
(somber classical music)

2178
01:26:30,553 --> 01:26:33,990
(hocks)

2179
01:26:34,023 --> 01:26:40,028
Ah!

2180
01:26:40,062 --> 01:26:43,800
Am I Liz Taylor yet?

2181
01:26:43,833 --> 01:26:47,403
(humming)

2182
01:26:47,437 --> 01:26:51,942
Ew, you snicker-snagged on me.

2183
01:26:51,975 --> 01:26:58,682
♪ Oh, sweet mystery of life,
at last I've found you.

2184
01:26:58,715 --> 01:27:01,883
Well, I am off to be destroyed.

2185
01:27:01,918 --> 01:27:04,853
Transport safely, Dick.

2186
01:27:04,887 --> 01:27:07,523
What was that all about?

2187
01:27:07,557 --> 01:27:09,158
Well, another
day, another dollar.

2188
01:27:09,192 --> 01:27:11,293
You can check out
anytime you like

2189
01:27:11,327 --> 01:27:13,863
but you can never leave.

2190
01:27:13,897 --> 01:27:17,700
Where'd I park that spaceship?

2191
01:27:17,733 --> 01:27:20,135
I was at the airport,
I was in a cab here,

2192
01:27:20,168 --> 01:27:24,107
that's all I saw.

2193
01:27:24,140 --> 01:27:25,408
I wonder if that tickles?

2194
01:27:25,442 --> 01:27:30,680
I bet it does.

2195
01:27:30,713 --> 01:27:32,915
Mork calling Olsen,
Mork calling Olsen.

2196
01:27:32,948 --> 01:27:38,253
Come in Olsen.

2197
01:27:38,287 --> 01:27:41,923
What a weird day.

2198
01:27:41,958 --> 01:27:43,660
Ah, ah, ah, ah,

2199
01:27:43,693 --> 01:27:45,828
Staying alive, staying alive.

2200
01:27:45,862 --> 01:27:47,963
Ah, ah...

2201
01:27:47,997 --> 01:27:50,265
Na noo, na noo.

2202
01:27:50,300 --> 01:27:51,267
(chuckles)

2203
01:27:51,300 --> 01:27:52,468
Finally, finally the end.

2204
01:27:52,502 --> 01:27:54,103
(all cheer)

2205
01:27:54,137 --> 01:28:00,275
Alright.

2206
01:28:00,310 --> 01:28:08,918
(doors creak and whir)

2207
01:28:08,952 --> 01:28:10,520
Well I think I liked
her best in the part

2208
01:28:10,553 --> 01:28:12,288
of blue shorty with
the matching tights.

2209
01:28:12,322 --> 01:28:13,657
Crow, you have
got your taste up--

2210
01:28:13,690 --> 01:28:15,592
Alright, enough,
enough you two.

2211
01:28:15,625 --> 01:28:16,993
You know, despite all
the really dumb things

2212
01:28:17,027 --> 01:28:18,260
in today's movie,

2213
01:28:18,293 --> 01:28:20,863
I thought it was really great
that Richard Kiel finally

2214
01:28:20,897 --> 01:28:22,798
came out in the
end and confessed

2215
01:28:22,832 --> 01:28:25,335
that he was indeed an android.

2216
01:28:25,368 --> 01:28:28,303
I mean, it's not like we
didn't know it all along

2217
01:28:28,337 --> 01:28:30,907
but just to have to the
moxie to come out and say,

2218
01:28:30,940 --> 01:28:34,277
"Hey, this is who I
am, and I'm proud."

2219
01:28:34,310 --> 01:28:36,112
It's pretty neat, really.

2220
01:28:36,145 --> 01:28:38,013
Yeah, well it was really
just a matter of time

2221
01:28:38,047 --> 01:28:39,948
before he had to come out.

2222
01:28:39,982 --> 01:28:43,652
Have you seen this week's
issue of Robot Nation?

2223
01:28:43,687 --> 01:28:46,588
Aha! You know I always had a
hunch about him.

2224
01:28:46,622 --> 01:28:48,758
Yup, look at that,
every one of them.

2225
01:28:48,792 --> 01:28:52,328
Tweaky, the girl from Small
Wonder, Robbie the Robot,

2226
01:28:52,362 --> 01:28:53,628
Al Gore.

2227
01:28:53,662 --> 01:28:55,732
You know, I hear that
having dinner with R2D2

2228
01:28:55,765 --> 01:28:56,898
is just like admitting it.

2229
01:28:56,932 --> 01:28:58,768
Admitting what?

2230
01:28:58,802 --> 01:29:01,837
Joel, Tom and I have
something to tell you.

2231
01:29:01,870 --> 01:29:04,040
You two got into my
sewing kit again?

2232
01:29:04,073 --> 01:29:07,777
Joel, Joel, Joel, I wish
things were still that simple.

2233
01:29:07,810 --> 01:29:11,013
But, well, this is something
I think we've all known

2234
01:29:11,047 --> 01:29:12,448
for a long time.

2235
01:29:12,482 --> 01:29:14,583
I know we've alluded to it.

2236
01:29:14,617 --> 01:29:18,453
A stilted joke here,
a fleeting doubt there,

2237
01:29:18,487 --> 01:29:21,590
and yet never have
we actually said,

2238
01:29:21,623 --> 01:29:29,032
"Joel, Tom and I..."

2239
01:29:29,065 --> 01:29:30,600
Oh for crying out in the beer,

2240
01:29:30,633 --> 01:29:33,168
Joel, Crow and I are robots

2241
01:29:33,202 --> 01:29:34,637
and we want the world to know.

2242
01:29:34,670 --> 01:29:36,072
Well, Tom I knew that.

2243
01:29:36,105 --> 01:29:37,973
Now, can we get on
with this letter?

2244
01:29:38,007 --> 01:29:40,977
Sure, but Joel, how
did you already know?

2245
01:29:41,010 --> 01:29:44,413
Tom, it's more than a
little obvious, alright?

2246
01:29:44,447 --> 01:29:45,313
It is?

2247
01:29:45,347 --> 01:29:47,117
Let's put this up
on still store there.

2248
01:29:47,150 --> 01:29:50,520
This one is from a Kevin Jones

2249
01:29:50,553 --> 01:29:53,455
and it's from
Ypsilanti, Michigan.

2250
01:29:53,488 --> 01:29:56,658
He says, "Dear Joel, I like
Mystery Science Theater,

2251
01:29:56,692 --> 01:29:59,462
I watch your show every
time I get a chance.

2252
01:29:59,495 --> 01:30:01,863
I was just watching your show,
it's the one about the ghost

2253
01:30:01,897 --> 01:30:06,168
who haunts Tom Stewart,
I just saw him die.

2254
01:30:06,202 --> 01:30:07,970
Well, I'll tell you a
little about myself,

2255
01:30:08,003 --> 01:30:10,973
I'm 11 years old, my
name is Kevin Jones,

2256
01:30:11,007 --> 01:30:12,608
so write back to me, okay?

2257
01:30:12,642 --> 01:30:14,143
Sincerely, Kevin Jones.

2258
01:30:14,177 --> 01:30:15,945
We certainly will, Kevin

2259
01:30:15,978 --> 01:30:17,647
and if you would
like to write to us,

2260
01:30:17,680 --> 01:30:20,415
send your letters to the
Mystery Science Theater 3000

2261
01:30:20,450 --> 01:30:23,285
information club,
post office box 5325

2262
01:30:23,318 --> 01:30:26,088
Hopkins, Minnesota 55343.

2263
01:30:26,122 --> 01:30:26,822
You tell him?

2264
01:30:26,855 --> 01:30:27,957
He knew.

2265
01:30:27,990 --> 01:30:29,092
What up, sirs?

2266
01:30:29,125 --> 01:30:30,993
(laughing)

2267
01:30:31,027 --> 01:30:33,930
William Conrad is
actually gonna be here.

2268
01:30:33,963 --> 01:30:36,465
Like Cannon is
going to show up here.

2269
01:30:36,498 --> 01:30:37,833
I'm sure.

2270
01:30:37,867 --> 01:30:39,668
(alarm blares)

2271
01:30:39,702 --> 01:30:41,803
Frank, it's the big one.

2272
01:30:41,837 --> 01:30:42,838
Literally.

2273
01:30:42,872 --> 01:30:44,173
After him.

2274
01:30:44,207 --> 01:30:47,143
Oh, come on, relax, chief.
He's not gonna get far.

2275
01:30:47,177 --> 01:30:50,145
How true, how true.

2276
01:30:50,178 --> 01:30:52,748
What say, in honor of the
occasion, I press the button

2277
01:30:52,782 --> 01:30:53,782
this week.

2278
01:30:53,817 --> 01:30:54,583
It would be an honor.

2279
01:30:54,717 --> 01:30:55,985
Thank you, Frank.
